1
00:00:03,670 --> 00:00:07,460
We brought along the guys
that got beat up by him yesterday.

2
00:00:07,460 --> 00:00:11,250
They'll tell you what happened,
and I think it'll make you reconsider his punishment.

3
00:00:13,170 --> 00:00:14,380
You guys...

4
00:00:14,750 --> 00:00:17,500
Come on. Hurry and cough it up, fellas.

5
00:00:18,130 --> 00:00:21,960
W-well, Nishiwaki gathered up
a whole group of us yesterday.

6
00:00:21,960 --> 00:00:26,040
He told us to lay the pressure on this
cocky freshman punk and get him to join our clique.

7
00:00:26,750 --> 00:00:30,630
Yo. Why the hell are you in here playing basketball?

8
00:00:30,630 --> 00:00:34,330
Don't you know that the Kuzu High basketball team
is just a bunch of trash?

9
00:00:34,710 --> 00:00:36,920
I'm Nishiwaki, a senior here.

10
00:00:36,920 --> 00:00:38,290
Nice to meetcha.

11
00:00:38,290 --> 00:00:40,170
You're a freshman, right Natsume?

12
00:00:40,420 --> 00:00:42,880
I'm gonna give you two options.

13
00:00:42,880 --> 00:00:44,880
Agree to be one of my followers now,

14
00:00:44,880 --> 00:00:47,250
or we beat the shit out of you until you do.

15
00:00:47,750 --> 00:00:49,210
Not interested.

16
00:00:50,330 --> 00:00:51,880
Get lost, dumbass.

17
00:00:55,630 --> 00:00:57,290
Don't play stupid with me.

18
00:00:57,290 --> 00:00:59,380
I told you to pick one, dammit.

19
00:00:59,630 --> 00:01:01,380
I don't need your bullshit!

20
00:01:02,250 --> 00:01:04,670
Do you get it now? Huh?

21
00:01:07,830 --> 00:01:11,000
After that, he totally snapped and we got flattened.

22
00:01:11,000 --> 00:01:13,040
Along with Nishiwaki and the rest.

23
00:01:27,830 --> 00:01:30,960
Where to go? The land, sea or sky?

24
00:01:30,130 --> 00:01:33,540
Ahiru no Sora

25
00:01:31,040 --> 00:01:34,000
I wanna invite you to come along

26
00:01:34,380 --> 00:01:38,830
The pages of our story have started to turn

27
00:01:41,170 --> 00:01:44,580
If you lose your nerve then recycle it

28
00:01:44,580 --> 00:01:47,580
And let it push you past hesitation

29
00:01:47,580 --> 00:01:52,790
Give and go! With the flow

30
00:01:55,380 --> 00:02:00,920
Instincts that are buried deep will always rear their head again

31
00:02:01,540 --> 00:02:08,130
People can't just hide the dreams they once dreamed of

32
00:02:08,460 --> 00:02:11,540
Even if these wings can't fly

33
00:02:11,540 --> 00:02:18,380
We want to spread them wide and embrace the sky

34
00:02:18,540 --> 00:02:21,710
Becoming the people who we want to be

35
00:02:21,880 --> 00:02:28,420
You never know, the impossible could be possible tomorrow

36
00:02:28,420 --> 00:02:31,880
So let's keep up the struggle

37
00:02:32,040 --> 00:02:34,920
Happy go ducky!

38
00:02:44,380 --> 00:02:47,040
So if the other guys started the whole fight,

39
00:02:45,750 --> 00:02:49,960
Kite, His Ball, and the Team's Pain

40
00:02:47,460 --> 00:02:49,960
that means it was self-defense! Right, teach?

41
00:02:50,420 --> 00:02:54,920
Natsume being expelled was based on the fact
that students were injured as a result of his actions.

42
00:02:55,460 --> 00:02:59,500
Even if it was in self-defense,
not all violent actions can be overlooked.

43
00:02:59,790 --> 00:03:02,290
Are you saying he should've just sat there and taken it?!

44
00:03:02,290 --> 00:03:05,170
Would you really do the same thing
in that situation, teach?!

45
00:03:06,000 --> 00:03:09,170
Some pain in life must be borne with. Remember that.

46
00:03:10,630 --> 00:03:11,960
Seriously?

47
00:03:11,960 --> 00:03:14,420
This is why I hate dealing with authority.

48
00:03:14,420 --> 00:03:17,380
We always get the short end of the damn stick.

49
00:03:17,920 --> 00:03:20,210
You guys are free to go now.

50
00:03:20,210 --> 00:03:21,330
Hold up.

51
00:03:21,330 --> 00:03:23,170
Tell that punk Nishiwaki when you get back...

52
00:03:23,460 --> 00:03:27,750
...that if he pulls this shit again,
then I'm gonna smash his face in personally.

53
00:03:31,040 --> 00:03:32,500
What's your deal?

54
00:03:33,290 --> 00:03:36,290
I never asked for or wanted any of your help.

55
00:03:36,290 --> 00:03:37,880
Keep your nose out of this.

56
00:03:38,170 --> 00:03:40,920
Look, I didn't come here trying to help you.

57
00:03:41,790 --> 00:03:44,130
I just wanted to wipe the slate clean.

58
00:03:44,130 --> 00:03:45,040
What?

59
00:03:47,170 --> 00:03:50,080
Your ball... I'm sorry that I kicked it.

60
00:03:50,880 --> 00:03:52,250
It's special to you, yeah?

61
00:03:55,580 --> 00:03:56,790
The hell does that mean?

62
00:03:57,790 --> 00:03:59,580
Quit making all this shit up.

63
00:04:00,790 --> 00:04:03,040
What was all that about, Yasuhara?

64
00:04:03,290 --> 00:04:07,750
Well, when we first met him, I picked up his ball
and kicked it without thinking.

65
00:04:08,670 --> 00:04:11,790
And his fight with Nishiwaki's group
was triggered by the same thing.

66
00:04:12,630 --> 00:04:16,880
Plus, when he accidentally hurt that girl,
it was only because he was so absorbed in basketball.

67
00:04:17,920 --> 00:04:20,210
It didn't take me long to figure it out.

68
00:04:21,040 --> 00:04:24,210
He's not a punk, just a dumbass
that loves playing basketball.

69
00:04:26,710 --> 00:04:28,380
AH! I JUST REMEMBERED!

70
00:04:28,580 --> 00:04:32,790
He promised to play basketball with us
if I managed to take the ball from him earlier!

71
00:04:40,710 --> 00:04:42,290
It's special to you, yeah?

72
00:04:43,420 --> 00:04:44,830
Hey, Kenji!

73
00:04:44,830 --> 00:04:47,330
What's this? You playin' basketball again?

74
00:04:53,420 --> 00:04:54,580
Hey! You!

75
00:04:55,790 --> 00:04:57,380
Y-you talking to me?

76
00:04:57,380 --> 00:04:59,080
Yeah, help me out!

77
00:04:59,380 --> 00:05:01,710
If you got any spare paper, I could really use it.

78
00:05:02,500 --> 00:05:04,790
Oh God, this dude is taking a shit...

79
00:05:07,330 --> 00:05:09,000
Boy, you really saved my ass!

80
00:05:09,000 --> 00:05:12,170
I called my little brother,
but it was already getting crusty down there!

81
00:05:12,330 --> 00:05:14,290
You, uh, can just keep them.

82
00:05:14,290 --> 00:05:16,080
It was a free pack of tissues, anyway.

83
00:05:16,080 --> 00:05:18,710
Oh yeah? I really appreciate it, man.

84
00:05:19,250 --> 00:05:21,790
By the way, that ball you have caught my eye earlier.

85
00:05:22,080 --> 00:05:23,710
Are you basketball player?

86
00:05:25,040 --> 00:05:28,380
I'm not so sure. I used to be, but maybe not anymore.

87
00:05:28,920 --> 00:05:31,080
The school I just entered is kind of a dump.

88
00:05:31,540 --> 00:05:33,790
There's not really a basketball team to speak of.

89
00:05:33,790 --> 00:05:36,040
Plus, I just got expelled anyway.

90
00:05:36,750 --> 00:05:38,790
I don't think I'll be playing much anymore.

91
00:05:40,330 --> 00:05:42,670
I've got... a lot of regrets.

92
00:05:43,210 --> 00:05:46,170
If you feel that way, then don't be a quitter
and just keep playing.

93
00:05:46,710 --> 00:05:47,630
Momoharu!

94
00:05:48,500 --> 00:05:50,790
Did you get a job as a toilet paper salesman or what?

95
00:05:50,790 --> 00:05:53,080
You're the one who told me
to go and buy some, dammit!

96
00:05:53,080 --> 00:05:54,710
You stupid shithead!

97
00:05:53,500 --> 00:05:55,790
This guy is his... little brother?

98
00:05:56,290 --> 00:05:57,920
"Kite" was your name, yeah?

99
00:05:58,330 --> 00:06:00,170
Have you already decided to quit going to school?

100
00:06:00,540 --> 00:06:02,460
That's none of your business.

101
00:06:04,080 --> 00:06:06,500
I know our basketball team is pretty shitty.

102
00:06:06,500 --> 00:06:10,630
All the skilled players hoping to join
always leave after taking a look at us.

103
00:06:10,920 --> 00:06:14,040
But you know, there was just one guy who didn't.

104
00:06:14,710 --> 00:06:16,830
How could you ever understand how I feel?

105
00:06:16,830 --> 00:06:19,380
Because I was in a similar spot until recently.

106
00:06:19,960 --> 00:06:23,380
Though, I don't know jack shit
about your personal problems.

107
00:06:24,710 --> 00:06:28,630
But you gave up before even starting,
so doesn't that make you the loser?

108
00:06:34,670 --> 00:06:36,170
Payphone

109
00:06:36,330 --> 00:06:38,290
Okay! I'm waiting!

110
00:06:42,830 --> 00:06:45,880
That's right... I am the loser.

111
00:06:50,750 --> 00:06:54,080
Come on, teach! Cut the guy some slack!

112
00:06:54,080 --> 00:06:55,580
I've heard enough from you.

113
00:06:55,880 --> 00:06:59,040
Natsume's punishment is final. Just give it up.

114
00:06:59,040 --> 00:07:02,670
That's why I'm here! I'm asking you
to please do something about it!

115
00:07:02,960 --> 00:07:05,170
I've never met someone this hard to get through to.

116
00:07:06,920 --> 00:07:09,130
Expelled students
need love, too

117
00:07:07,250 --> 00:07:09,080
Please and thank you!

118
00:07:11,170 --> 00:07:13,630
I'm beggin' you, Teach!

119
00:07:14,500 --> 00:07:15,710
I find this hard to understand.

120
00:07:16,420 --> 00:07:19,080
You and Natsume aren't even
on very good terms, are you?

121
00:07:19,080 --> 00:07:20,960
Why go so far to cover for him?

122
00:07:21,540 --> 00:07:24,500
I will admit that I don't really like the guy.

123
00:07:24,500 --> 00:07:25,920
He's way too violent.

124
00:07:25,920 --> 00:07:28,210
And his haircut makes him look like melon bread.

125
00:07:28,630 --> 00:07:29,420
But...

126
00:07:30,330 --> 00:07:32,790
I absolutely adore his basketball skills.

127
00:07:33,250 --> 00:07:34,460
That's why...

128
00:07:35,670 --> 00:07:37,790
Quit being a creep, dummy.

129
00:07:41,130 --> 00:07:43,330
I've been looking for you, Mr. Satsuki.

130
00:07:44,170 --> 00:07:47,460
Please, Teach. I want you to reverse
the decision to expel me.

131
00:07:47,960 --> 00:07:48,960
What did you say?

132
00:07:50,080 --> 00:07:51,630
Don't be absurd.

133
00:07:51,630 --> 00:07:53,670
It's too late to change your punishment.

134
00:07:53,670 --> 00:07:55,330
I don't expect it for free.

135
00:07:55,330 --> 00:07:57,080
I'll make this school famous.

136
00:07:57,380 --> 00:08:00,290
And as our advisor, you'll get to reap plenty of benefits.

137
00:08:01,170 --> 00:08:01,960
What?

138
00:08:03,250 --> 00:08:07,000
I'll take the Kuzu High basketball team...
all the way to the inter-high nationals.

139
00:08:07,630 --> 00:08:08,500
Huh?

140
00:08:10,290 --> 00:08:13,630
I thought you didn't want to be associated
with the basketball team.

141
00:08:14,080 --> 00:08:16,000
What caused you to change your mind?

142
00:08:16,750 --> 00:08:20,580
I guess I spent too much time around these idiots
and caught a case of the stupid.

143
00:08:21,170 --> 00:08:23,630
I know I'm making a selfish request.

144
00:08:23,630 --> 00:08:27,210
But I can't just turn tail and give up on everything now.

145
00:08:28,290 --> 00:08:31,750
Please! Just give me one more chance!

146
00:08:32,580 --> 00:08:33,960
You're being ridiculous.

147
00:08:35,290 --> 00:08:39,040
And it's pointless to even bring this up
with me in the first place.

148
00:08:39,040 --> 00:08:41,460
Because I have no authority in your case.

149
00:08:41,830 --> 00:08:43,080
You need to accept the facts and gi-

150
00:08:43,080 --> 00:08:45,330
Very well, then allow me to decide.

151
00:08:46,250 --> 00:08:48,630
The Kuzu High team going to the inter-high nationals?

152
00:08:48,790 --> 00:08:51,420
That's quite the promising prospect, if you ask me.

153
00:08:52,670 --> 00:08:53,710
Who's that?

154
00:08:54,080 --> 00:08:55,290
Mr. Principal!

155
00:08:57,630 --> 00:08:58,750
So without further ado,

156
00:08:58,750 --> 00:09:00,710
I'll be introducing the newest member of the team.

157
00:09:00,920 --> 00:09:01,540
Natsume Kenj-

158
00:09:01,540 --> 00:09:02,750
I'm Kite.

159
00:09:02,750 --> 00:09:04,170
I look forward to playing with you.

160
00:09:04,500 --> 00:09:08,460
Everything worked out, but only because
the Principal made a special exception in your case.

161
00:09:08,750 --> 00:09:11,710
But do not forget that the conditions
on which the team can play remain the same.

162
00:09:12,210 --> 00:09:14,830
None of this means that I've got any personal faith in you.

163
00:09:14,830 --> 00:09:16,130
I get it.

164
00:09:16,330 --> 00:09:18,330
I'm done. No more fights.

165
00:09:18,670 --> 00:09:20,540
All right! Time for practice.

166
00:09:28,960 --> 00:09:31,790
Your dribbling is still amazing
no matter how many times I see it.

167
00:09:31,790 --> 00:09:34,920
How the hell do you hold the ball
to move it around so freely like that?

168
00:09:35,380 --> 00:09:38,170
Nah, you don't hold it. You stick to it.

169
00:09:38,670 --> 00:09:40,380
You said it yourself, remember?

170
00:09:41,130 --> 00:09:43,830
It was almost as if the ball
was glued to your hand or something.

171
00:09:44,460 --> 00:09:48,920
You can't just force the ball down,
you also have to lead it as it comes back up.

172
00:09:49,500 --> 00:09:52,960
Of course, the ball won't actually stick to you
even if you're pulling it along.

173
00:09:53,210 --> 00:09:55,630
The important thing is simply to maintain that image of it.

174
00:09:55,790 --> 00:09:57,500
Cool. I think I get it.

175
00:09:57,500 --> 00:10:01,130
When you get the hang of it, switch to your left hand.

176
00:10:01,130 --> 00:10:03,880
And once you can do that,
then you use both hands. Two balls at once.

177
00:10:03,290 --> 00:10:04,420
Mom.

178
00:10:03,880 --> 00:10:06,460
Both hands?! That's gotta be impossible.

179
00:10:04,420 --> 00:10:07,420
There are just so many amazing people in the world!

180
00:10:06,460 --> 00:10:09,080
It's possible. Just watch this.

181
00:10:08,210 --> 00:10:12,920
He made me realize that I've barely even
scratched the surface of the world of basketball!

182
00:10:09,080 --> 00:10:11,250
Holy shit! You're amazing, dude.

183
00:10:13,330 --> 00:10:16,290
Kanagawa School of Medical Science
Secondary Hospital

184
00:10:13,750 --> 00:10:16,040
I was a little worried that we might get disbanded.

185
00:10:16,330 --> 00:10:18,380
But now our team has an awesome lineup of members!

186
00:10:19,170 --> 00:10:20,500
The cherry blossoms...

187
00:10:20,670 --> 00:10:22,580
have already wilted away this year.

188
00:10:22,580 --> 00:10:24,630
Well, April went by pretty quickly.

189
00:10:27,250 --> 00:10:29,210
Oh, I can smell rain!

190
00:10:30,330 --> 00:10:32,710
It doesn't seem like a storm is coming to me.

191
00:10:32,710 --> 00:10:34,790
It will. Really soon.

192
00:10:38,380 --> 00:10:42,290
Rain, huh? I hate when it rains.
I always end up slipping on the court.

193
00:10:42,290 --> 00:10:45,420
But we can't even use the court today,
which means practice is outside.

194
00:10:45,420 --> 00:10:47,250
That makes me hate the rain even more.

195
00:10:47,790 --> 00:10:50,500
Although, it's not like our team
has even had proper training to begin with.

196
00:10:50,500 --> 00:10:53,420
Which means days like this would be the prefect chance
to spend time building muscle instead.

197
00:10:54,210 --> 00:10:57,040
And Mr. Satsuki doesn't really know anything
about basketball, anyway.

198
00:10:57,040 --> 00:11:00,250
What we need now is someone who can figure out
a training schedule for us to keep...

199
00:11:07,540 --> 00:11:11,330
Today I'm pulling out all the stops to make sure
you get the beating that you deserve.

200
00:11:11,330 --> 00:11:12,670
Brace yourself.

201
00:11:13,960 --> 00:11:15,330
Now get up, dammit!

202
00:11:15,750 --> 00:11:18,580
What's the deal? You're not putting up
much of a fight this time.

203
00:11:18,580 --> 00:11:21,380
And here I went out of my way to gather up
all these extra guys.

204
00:11:21,750 --> 00:11:22,790
At least let us have a little fun-

205
00:11:22,790 --> 00:11:24,130
My ball...

206
00:11:24,880 --> 00:11:26,380
Don't touch... my ball...

207
00:11:27,210 --> 00:11:28,880
Don't fuck with me, punk!

208
00:11:32,540 --> 00:11:35,750
Y'know, I hear the basketball team
has gotten serious about playing lately.

209
00:11:35,750 --> 00:11:39,210
Apparently, they got permission
on the condition that they don't cause any trouble.

210
00:11:39,210 --> 00:11:42,330
Huh? Is that what's holding this little idiot back?

211
00:11:42,750 --> 00:11:44,920
Well that sounds all sorts of fun.

212
00:11:44,920 --> 00:11:47,710
If we get this guy to snap,
then the basketball team is finished.

213
00:11:48,130 --> 00:11:50,830
And they've all been getting
on my nerves for a while now.

214
00:11:50,830 --> 00:11:52,460
Especially those damn twins.

215
00:11:52,710 --> 00:11:54,040
Come on, do it.

216
00:11:54,040 --> 00:11:56,130
I'll let you take a totally free swing at me.

217
00:11:56,130 --> 00:11:59,080
So just let the basketball team rot and die, okay?

218
00:11:59,750 --> 00:12:02,040
No skin off our bones, Kite. Let him have it.

219
00:12:02,250 --> 00:12:03,830
I'll even help if you want.

220
00:12:04,460 --> 00:12:06,170
Y-Yasuhara, you little bitch!

221
00:12:06,170 --> 00:12:10,420
We can avoid being disbanded if we just get rid
of the evidence after we beat the snot out of you turds!

222
00:12:10,670 --> 00:12:11,670
That's right.

223
00:12:11,670 --> 00:12:14,210
We can sweep it all under the rug after the fact.

224
00:12:14,790 --> 00:12:17,830
But first, I wanna know which of you jerks
sent this ball raining down on me!

225
00:12:18,420 --> 00:12:22,670
Uh... why don't you just go home and watch TV
with an afternoon snack or somethin'. Okay?

226
00:12:22,670 --> 00:12:26,290
Why should I do that?! I can hold my own!
I'll take 'em to the cleaners!

227
00:12:26,290 --> 00:12:29,040
I'll piledrive whoever threw this ball right into the dirt!

228
00:12:29,250 --> 00:12:30,630
I don't need any help.

229
00:12:31,630 --> 00:12:32,960
Just shut up and watch.

230
00:12:34,330 --> 00:12:37,210
I don't even need to use my hands
to deal with losers like you.

231
00:12:37,210 --> 00:12:39,130
Come on, do your worst.

232
00:12:39,580 --> 00:12:41,750
You cheeky punk! I'll make you regret that!

233
00:12:47,250 --> 00:12:49,670
Stupid freshman like you don't get to talk back!

234
00:12:49,670 --> 00:12:50,830
Eat shit and die!

235
00:12:51,420 --> 00:12:52,460
Hold on, Kite!

236
00:12:52,670 --> 00:12:53,710
Stay out of it.

237
00:12:55,040 --> 00:12:58,040
He's doing exactly what Satsuki told us we'd have to.

238
00:12:58,040 --> 00:12:58,960
For real.

239
00:12:59,130 --> 00:13:02,130
Some pain in life must be borne with. Remember that.

240
00:13:02,540 --> 00:13:06,540
Right now, he's bearing all the pain
so that the basketball team can survive.

241
00:13:06,540 --> 00:13:07,830
Kite...

242
00:13:07,830 --> 00:13:09,250
That dumbass!

243
00:13:09,540 --> 00:13:11,080
And it's our responsibility...

244
00:13:11,540 --> 00:13:14,460
...to bear the pain of having
to watch him get beat up like this!

245
00:13:15,710 --> 00:13:17,250
What are you boys doing?!

246
00:13:17,250 --> 00:13:18,460
Shit, it's Satsuki!

247
00:13:18,460 --> 00:13:19,380
Run for it!

248
00:13:20,330 --> 00:13:21,630
Hold it! Stop right there!

249
00:13:24,330 --> 00:13:26,500
Is fighting all those boys know how to do?!

250
00:13:26,500 --> 00:13:27,670
For God's sake.

251
00:13:28,880 --> 00:13:30,170
That goes for all of you, too!

252
00:13:30,170 --> 00:13:32,670
As if you didn't cause enough trouble
with everything yesterday!

253
00:13:33,460 --> 00:13:35,710
Listen up. The basketball team will now be-

254
00:13:35,710 --> 00:13:37,710
Except we didn't cause any problems.

255
00:13:37,710 --> 00:13:38,920
At least not this time.

256
00:13:39,500 --> 00:13:40,460
Oh really?

257
00:13:42,080 --> 00:13:43,170
Hey, Teach.

258
00:13:44,710 --> 00:13:49,500
I thought maybe I could figure out...
the meaning of what you said yesterday, Mr. Satsuki.

259
00:13:50,000 --> 00:13:51,210
But honestly...

260
00:13:51,460 --> 00:13:54,790
...I don't think this whole "bear the pain"
thing is such a good fit for me.

261
00:13:56,880 --> 00:13:59,170
Same here. I thought I was gonna have a heart attack.

262
00:13:59,170 --> 00:14:00,080
You said it.

263
00:14:00,080 --> 00:14:01,710
Yeah, screw that noise.

264
00:14:02,210 --> 00:14:03,580
W-wait a moment!

265
00:14:05,960 --> 00:14:07,130
What now?

266
00:14:10,000 --> 00:14:12,630
I can't say no to eyes like those. Good grief.

267
00:14:14,210 --> 00:14:17,040
From what I understand, the volleyball team
will be taking a break from practice today.

268
00:14:17,040 --> 00:14:20,040
If you wish to use the court,
then you can have free reign of it.

269
00:14:20,210 --> 00:14:21,040
Huh?

270
00:14:21,420 --> 00:14:22,670
Sweet!

271
00:14:22,880 --> 00:14:25,210
We can have a real practice session in the gym! Yahoo!

272
00:14:25,210 --> 00:14:25,920
Yo.
We can have a real practice session in the gym! Yahoo!

273
00:14:26,960 --> 00:14:27,960
Need a hand?

274
00:14:29,540 --> 00:14:31,130
I can't believe this.

275
00:14:31,290 --> 00:14:34,920
Your adorable new teammate was getting beat on,
and you all just stood there like rocks.

276
00:14:34,920 --> 00:14:37,330
You were the one who told us to shut up and watch!

277
00:14:37,330 --> 00:14:38,880
That was a figure of speech.

278
00:14:41,460 --> 00:14:43,330
It finally stopped raining.

279
00:14:43,330 --> 00:14:46,460
Okay, boys. Time to get pumped and start practicin'!

280
00:14:49,080 --> 00:14:51,250
Whoa, Kite! What's up with your face?!

281
00:14:51,250 --> 00:14:52,380
Don't tell me you got into another fight!

282
00:14:52,380 --> 00:14:53,750
Wasn't a fight.

283
00:14:53,750 --> 00:14:54,880
Not at all.

284
00:14:54,880 --> 00:14:55,880
Probably.

285
00:14:55,880 --> 00:14:57,710
But who can say for sure?

286
00:14:57,710 --> 00:14:59,080
Does it really even matter?

287
00:15:00,630 --> 00:15:01,880
So, hey.

288
00:15:02,880 --> 00:15:04,880
I've been curious this whole time.

289
00:15:04,880 --> 00:15:07,080
Why exactly do you go by "Kite"?

290
00:15:07,290 --> 00:15:08,750
Isn't your name "Kenji Natsume"?

291
00:15:10,460 --> 00:15:13,630
Cuz my dad was like a black kite,
up in the scaffolds at his job.

292
00:15:14,290 --> 00:15:15,460
He "was"?

293
00:15:16,420 --> 00:15:17,500
He's dead now.

294
00:15:18,750 --> 00:15:22,920
He was working one day, when a sudden gust of wind
blew away the scaffolding he was on.

295
00:15:23,170 --> 00:15:25,290
It was a headlong dive down 10 stories.

296
00:15:26,170 --> 00:15:27,330
Dad...

297
00:15:28,040 --> 00:15:29,920
Hey, Ken, we found this.

298
00:15:30,080 --> 00:15:32,630
It was mixed in with all your dad's other stuff.

299
00:15:38,250 --> 00:15:39,960
I want a legit basketball!

300
00:15:39,960 --> 00:15:42,080
One of those fancy ones made from real leather!

301
00:15:42,080 --> 00:15:44,960
Our family doesn't have that kind of money! Ya dummy!

302
00:15:47,330 --> 00:15:50,250
It happened just three days before my birthday.

303
00:15:51,210 --> 00:15:53,290
He was a cheapskate that drank a ton of booze,

304
00:15:53,630 --> 00:15:55,420
but he was always a good father to me.

305
00:15:56,040 --> 00:16:00,080
I never saw eye-to-eye with my new dad who
came along, and we just ended up fighting all the time.

306
00:16:00,580 --> 00:16:01,960
I see now.

307
00:16:01,960 --> 00:16:04,380
That's why he treasures that ball so much.

308
00:16:05,130 --> 00:16:07,290
Yo. I'm glad you're getting along with us and all.

309
00:16:07,830 --> 00:16:10,670
But I think there's one more
important thing you've still gotta do.

310
00:16:11,710 --> 00:16:14,540
Go and apologize to Yoshino on the volleyball team.

311
00:16:14,540 --> 00:16:15,670
You owe her that.

312
00:16:16,540 --> 00:16:17,750
No worries.

313
00:16:19,380 --> 00:16:21,170
We're real close friends now.

314
00:16:21,170 --> 00:16:22,670
In body and soul.

315
00:16:22,670 --> 00:16:25,670
Oh my gosh! Don't embarrass me, Kite!

316
00:16:25,670 --> 00:16:27,420
I made you lunch today!

317
00:16:28,670 --> 00:16:30,170
Oh, hey, Bro!

318
00:16:30,670 --> 00:16:32,670
You know, this means war.

319
00:16:33,080 --> 00:16:33,880
Huh?

320
00:16:34,210 --> 00:16:39,040
Because Yoshino was number 8 on my list of girls
who I most wanted to start dating!

321
00:16:39,380 --> 00:16:41,000
FACE MY DIVINE WRATH!

322
00:16:49,670 --> 00:16:50,500
So fast!

323
00:16:51,170 --> 00:16:53,750
I'm honestly surprised he's keeping up with my speed.

324
00:16:54,040 --> 00:16:55,500
This shrimp is pretty good.

325
00:16:57,250 --> 00:16:58,540
Okay, this is the last run!

326
00:16:58,710 --> 00:16:59,540
Pass it over to me!

327
00:17:04,710 --> 00:17:07,290
Hey, Tinytown. Wait a damn minute!

328
00:17:08,210 --> 00:17:09,670
Have you lost your mind?

329
00:17:09,830 --> 00:17:13,210
Who stops during a 2-man drill
to take a shot in the middle like that?

330
00:17:13,210 --> 00:17:15,460
You don't have to worry about me!

331
00:17:15,790 --> 00:17:17,790
I promise I won't miss any of my shots!

332
00:17:18,250 --> 00:17:20,380
That's not the problem here.

333
00:17:20,500 --> 00:17:21,710
Damn this little shrimp.

334
00:17:21,710 --> 00:17:24,000
The level of accuracy his shots have is unbelievable...

335
00:17:24,460 --> 00:17:27,000
Still, our practice sessions have only been
the same thing over and over.

336
00:17:27,330 --> 00:17:29,380
Don't you have anything else that we can do, Captain?

337
00:17:29,380 --> 00:17:30,920
You want some other drills?

338
00:17:31,250 --> 00:17:32,330
Yo, Teach.

339
00:17:32,710 --> 00:17:34,830
Quit staring and try actually coaching us for once.

340
00:17:35,080 --> 00:17:36,330
You're our advisor, right?

341
00:17:36,580 --> 00:17:37,830
That's true.

342
00:17:38,250 --> 00:17:40,670
Then... how about you do some running?

343
00:17:44,290 --> 00:17:46,750
Dammit, Momoharu. You and your big fat mouth.

344
00:17:47,420 --> 00:17:49,080
Um, Momoharu?

345
00:17:49,500 --> 00:17:53,630
I think we really need someone to help research
and plan a training schedule for us.

346
00:17:54,290 --> 00:17:56,710
You're right. I'll think about it.

347
00:17:57,460 --> 00:17:59,500
Okay, that's enough for today.

348
00:18:00,330 --> 00:18:03,170
He must be trying to kill us, making us run 500 laps...

349
00:18:03,170 --> 00:18:04,540
Oh, I nearly forgot.

350
00:18:04,880 --> 00:18:08,880
This really doesn't pertain to any of you,
but the match schedule for the first semester is out.

351
00:18:08,880 --> 00:18:10,250
Here's a copy of it for reference.

352
00:18:11,500 --> 00:18:14,960
Crap, do the inter-high prelims
really start at the end of May?

353
00:18:14,960 --> 00:18:16,960
We barely have a month left to practice, then!

354
00:18:16,960 --> 00:18:20,170
Wow! There's also a tournament
just for the Kanto region!

355
00:18:20,170 --> 00:18:22,210
That would be fun, I hope we can participate!

356
00:18:22,630 --> 00:18:24,880
We're too late to have any hope of entering that.

357
00:18:24,880 --> 00:18:26,670
The second round of games starts tomorrow.

358
00:18:26,670 --> 00:18:28,040
Gah, you're right...

359
00:18:28,040 --> 00:18:29,250
That sucks.

360
00:18:31,040 --> 00:18:32,040
Oh!

361
00:18:32,040 --> 00:18:34,580
Then let's go watch it! Together!

362
00:18:34,580 --> 00:18:36,750
No way. That's too much effort, man.

363
00:18:37,580 --> 00:18:40,290
I wanna go! Let's go!

364
00:18:43,880 --> 00:18:46,460
Jeez! I can't believe how late you guys are!

365
00:18:46,710 --> 00:18:50,130
I said we would meet up at 10 this morning,
but you kept me waiting for 4 hours!

366
00:18:50,460 --> 00:18:54,500
Now we'll be lucky to even catch
the last quarter of the final game of the day!

367
00:18:54,750 --> 00:18:55,960
Don't sweat it.

368
00:18:56,460 --> 00:19:00,040
Ugh... I should have just gone with Kite
when he left earlier.

369
00:19:00,330 --> 00:19:02,920
Seeing the final game of this round is more than enough.

370
00:19:02,920 --> 00:19:05,830
Just look, I did some research online yesterday.

371
00:19:06,080 --> 00:19:07,420
This is today's matchup.

372
00:19:09,250 --> 00:19:11,250
This must be some kind of fate.

373
00:19:11,670 --> 00:19:13,290
ABSOLUTE VICTORY

374
00:19:12,080 --> 00:19:19,460
Defense! Defense! Defense! Defense...!

375
00:19:20,170 --> 00:19:21,080
A steal...

376
00:19:21,290 --> 00:19:22,330
Dammit!

377
00:19:25,000 --> 00:19:27,960
Eirin
Shinmaruko

378
00:19:25,630 --> 00:19:27,630
Blocking! #4 on Defense!

379
00:19:28,250 --> 00:19:31,630
Maru High is losing... by 9 points even...

380
00:19:32,210 --> 00:19:36,040
Whoa! According to this,
their opponents right now are a seeded team.

381
00:19:32,670 --> 00:19:35,250
Charged timeout! Shinmaruko!

382
00:19:36,040 --> 00:19:38,880
They were ranked in the top 8
of last year's Kanto region tournament!

383
00:19:39,290 --> 00:19:43,080
We thought Maru High was tough as nails,
but even they're getting trashed out there.

384
00:19:43,290 --> 00:19:46,540
Do you guys really think we can compete
in matches like these?

385
00:19:44,420 --> 00:20:08,330
MA-RU-KO! MA-RU-KO! MA-RU-KO...!

386
00:19:50,290 --> 00:19:51,540
Hang in there, Maruko!

387
00:19:51,540 --> 00:19:52,880
You can do it!

388
00:19:57,250 --> 00:19:58,380
This game...

389
00:19:59,040 --> 00:20:00,960
...they still have a chance to turn it around.

390
00:20:00,960 --> 00:20:02,000
Huh?

391
00:20:02,540 --> 00:20:04,040
They ain't dead yet.

392
00:20:04,830 --> 00:20:08,330
Listen up, Choji! I want you to stick to their #10 like glue!

393
00:20:08,330 --> 00:20:09,080
Got it!

394
00:20:09,080 --> 00:20:12,380
Sawa! If you get the ball and have an open shot,
always go for the three!

395
00:20:12,670 --> 00:20:15,250
Even if you miss, I will DEFINITELY get the rebound!

396
00:20:15,250 --> 00:20:17,380
Just leave everything that happens
inside the paint to me!

397
00:20:17,630 --> 00:20:18,460
It's Chiba!

398
00:20:18,460 --> 00:20:20,880
He's as passionate as ever. Totally on fire.

399
00:20:24,040 --> 00:20:25,710
They're facing a full court press!

400
00:20:25,830 --> 00:20:27,920
The other team doesn't want
Maru High scoring any points!

401
00:20:30,380 --> 00:20:31,420
Tokiwa!

402
00:20:35,790 --> 00:20:36,540
He's quick.

403
00:20:37,210 --> 00:20:38,130
Here he comes!

404
00:20:38,130 --> 00:20:38,880
Cover him!

405
00:20:46,790 --> 00:20:48,500
Holy crap! He dunked it!

406
00:20:48,500 --> 00:20:50,460
I've never seen a dunk in a high school game before!

407
00:20:50,460 --> 00:20:52,290
That #4 is so cool!

408
00:20:51,000 --> 00:20:52,290
Nice, Chiba!

409
00:20:56,000 --> 00:20:58,130
This isn't good, he looks totally wiped.

410
00:20:58,130 --> 00:21:00,880
He didn't even need a dunk to score on that play.

411
00:21:01,130 --> 00:21:04,580
Yeah, that dude really only has
to raise his hand to reach the basket.

412
00:21:05,000 --> 00:21:07,250
It looks like he's just wasting precious stamina to me.

413
00:21:07,790 --> 00:21:09,080
He knows what he's doing.

414
00:21:09,710 --> 00:21:12,830
There's no denying that the other team
is slightly better than they are.

415
00:21:13,170 --> 00:21:16,960
But that only matters if they were playing
on completely even terms.

416
00:21:17,290 --> 00:21:18,750
What do you mean?

417
00:21:18,750 --> 00:21:19,630
Take a look.

418
00:21:20,920 --> 00:21:22,540
Just a few more points to take the lead!

419
00:21:20,920 --> 00:21:37,000
MA-RU-KO! MA-RU-KO! MA-RU-KO...!

420
00:21:22,750 --> 00:21:23,960
Don't give up!

421
00:21:25,170 --> 00:21:27,580
Even if he pushed his stamina to its absolute limit,

422
00:21:28,170 --> 00:21:30,290
that's a cheap price to pay
for turning the momentum in their favor.

423
00:21:32,210 --> 00:21:36,130
In moments like these, it becomes very clear
which team the crowd favors.

424
00:21:37,000 --> 00:21:40,540
And that is exactly when comebacks
are most likely to happen.

425
00:21:41,790 --> 00:21:45,130
That #4 down there, he really knows
how to play the game of basketball.

426
00:21:45,130 --> 00:21:46,710
There's no doubt his team is strong.

427
00:21:47,040 --> 00:21:52,250
Shinmaruko
Eirin

428
00:21:47,460 --> 00:21:48,790
The game is over!

429
00:21:49,330 --> 00:21:52,250
Insane! A total unknown managed
to beat a seeded team!

430
00:21:52,580 --> 00:21:54,040
H-hot damn...

431
00:21:54,040 --> 00:21:56,000
Those were some really sick moves.

432
00:21:56,540 --> 00:21:58,750
I wanna be able to dominate the court just like them!

433
00:22:02,920 --> 00:22:04,920
Yo! You were watching?

434
00:22:03,040 --> 00:22:06,380
It didn't matter how long you stared up at the sky

435
00:22:05,380 --> 00:22:07,580
That was kind of an embarrassing game for us.

436
00:22:06,380 --> 00:22:09,670
You always said that you would never be able to fly

437
00:22:08,170 --> 00:22:11,630
If we're struggling this much against a team
that hardly made the top 8 in Kanto,

438
00:22:09,670 --> 00:22:12,880
One night I cried wondering how long it would take

439
00:22:11,630 --> 00:22:13,790
it doesn't really bode well for our future.

440
00:22:13,040 --> 00:22:16,250
Until I could finally reach you with my hands

441
00:22:14,330 --> 00:22:18,330
As you can see, Kanagawa has the most intense
block of competition in the entire country.

442
00:22:16,380 --> 00:22:19,750
Eventually I got used to just running away

443
00:22:18,790 --> 00:22:20,630
Are you guys ready to get in on this?

444
00:22:19,750 --> 00:22:23,000
Until the day I realized that was a weakness

445
00:22:21,670 --> 00:22:26,250
For the time being, we're going to get a head start
on you by claiming the throne of Kanto.

446
00:22:23,000 --> 00:22:27,210
So let's start it all over, right now

447
00:22:26,880 --> 00:22:28,920
If you waste too much time, we'll leave you in the dust.

448
00:22:29,790 --> 00:22:32,250
We'll be right on your heels. Don't worry.

449
00:22:29,830 --> 00:22:35,880
The things precious to us were always close at hand

450
00:22:33,130 --> 00:22:35,750
If our school is also in the Kanagawa block,

451
00:22:35,750 --> 00:22:38,670
that means we can't reach the prefectural
prelims without beating Maru High.

452
00:22:35,880 --> 00:22:42,210
We are never completely alone at any time in our lives

453
00:22:39,170 --> 00:22:40,750
What do you think, Chiaki?

454
00:22:41,080 --> 00:22:43,920
I say the bigger the challenge, the greater the reward.

455
00:22:42,210 --> 00:22:45,540
The truth is that you can fly, wherever you want

456
00:22:45,040 --> 00:22:46,170
Damn straight.

457
00:22:45,540 --> 00:22:49,290
Spreading your wings to go far higher than anyone else

458
00:22:47,040 --> 00:22:49,330
You sure sent me to one hell of a place.

459
00:22:49,500 --> 00:22:53,540
The more tears that you shed

460
00:22:50,250 --> 00:22:51,750
I'm cursing you, Dad.

461
00:22:51,920 --> 00:22:54,210
I swear... this might kill me.

462
00:22:53,750 --> 00:22:55,500
Then the stronger you become

463
00:22:55,500 --> 00:22:58,880
Let's use those wings to travel the world over

464
00:22:56,920 --> 00:23:01,880
It really sucks to admit, but we can't even stand
on equal ground with Maru High as we are now.

465
00:22:58,880 --> 00:23:02,460
And find a path to a future that no one knows about

466
00:23:02,420 --> 00:23:04,170
I'm gonna need way more practice.

467
00:23:02,460 --> 00:23:07,000
Always, always, always

468
00:23:04,630 --> 00:23:06,880
I ain't quitting until my shots
start going in the damn basket!

469
00:23:07,170 --> 00:23:10,670
Walking onwards, all of us together

470
00:23:07,420 --> 00:23:08,830
I'd kill for some ice cream...

471
00:23:10,750 --> 00:23:12,460
Faster, stronger...

472
00:23:12,460 --> 00:23:14,080
We gotta keep getting better!

473
00:23:16,210 --> 00:23:18,750
Uh, so where exactly are we right now?

474
00:23:19,500 --> 00:23:21,420
Sorry. I put us on the wrong train.

475
00:23:23,710 --> 00:23:25,080
What do we do now?!

476
00:23:23,710 --> 00:23:30,960
ENOSHIMA BRIDGE

477
00:23:25,080 --> 00:23:27,000
I don't have anymore money left!

478
00:23:27,000 --> 00:23:28,500
Okay boys, we're running home.

479
00:23:28,500 --> 00:23:29,920
Are you serious?!

480
00:23:30,960 --> 00:23:35,420
Ahiru no Sora
Next Time: Manager

481
00:23:31,830 --> 00:23:34,330
Next time: "Manager."

